<title>UK: UK PSBR 8.80 bln stg in March.</title>
<headline>UK PSBR 8.80 bln stg in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK public sector borrowing requirement data for March. Deficits unless noted (rep).</p>
<p> PSBR (in million stg)	    MARCH    1996/97    1995/96</p>
<p> Public sector		     8,795    22,806     31,684</p>
<p> Central government		7,281    25,070     35,463</p>
<p> Central government own acct   7,247    24,879     35,776</p>
<p> Local Authority		     244	 548rep  1,145rep</p>
<p>   from central govt		 18rep  1,502	   473</p>
<p> General Government		7,543    23,020     33,845</p>
<p> Public Corporation		1,304    1,525rep  2,947rep</p>
<p>   from central govt		  52    1,311rep    786rep</p>
<p>NOTE - Forecast was 9.3 billion stg PSBR. Rep=repayment</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT RECEIPTS</p>
<p> Central govt total receipts   18,377    261,055    244,702</p>
<p> Inland Revenue receipts	  7,180    103,957     97,120</p>
<p>  of which income tax	     5,760     69,396     68,060</p>
<p>  corporation tax		     467     27,654     23,569</p>
<p> Customs and excise		 4,814     82,371     76,670</p>
<p>  of which VAT			2,119     46,854     43,073</p>
<p> Social security		    3,773     44,948     42,882</p>
<p> Interest			     1,593	8,323	8,660</p>
<p> Other				  1,017     21,456     19,370</p>
<p>CENTRAL GOVERNMENT OUTLAYS</p>
<p>  Total				25,624    285,934    280,478</p>
<p>   of which Interest		1,917     26,668     23,443</p>
<p>   Net departmental outlays    23,952    263,700    259,470</p>
<p>NOTE- Privatisation proceeds in March were 245 million stg, compared with 139 million in March last year.</p>
<p>The ONS said the March PSBR was reduced by 500 million stg by the first installment from the sale of the Housing Corporation loan book.</p>
</text>
